commit(k,t,rows,[('M0541','first','Soient','The word has the extra e/n strokes before its final t.','page','high'),('M0542','first',r'\deleted{Y}\inserted{Z}','Z is the replacement over the surviving fork of Y.',Z,'high')],['text|top|Axiome supplémentaire','display|axiom|M5 ∀n M_n stable par réunions finies','display|equivalent form|∅∈M_n and A∪B∈M_n','deletion|inside equivalent form|uncertain δ','text|first proposition|Parties modérées … stable …','text|second proposition|Sur ∅ … objet initial','text|third proposition|Soient X … famille finie …','insertion|after map|entre espaces modérés','text|question heading|Question Donnons-nous','diagram|lower centre|Z hooks to X1 and X2','deletion|diagram source|Y overwritten','insertion|diagram source|Z','text|question continuation|existe-t-il une somme amalgamée? Si Y=∅ …','margin note|foot|9'],"""Defines a new use of M5: closure of every M_n under finite unions, including the empty union. This is a reuse of the label previously assigned to R0≠∅ on scan 007, not an equality of the two assertions. The first two propositions assert finite-union stability for moderate subsets and a unique moderate structure on the empty set making it initial. The third gives gluing along a finite moderate cover. The final question asks whether pushouts of the two displayed embeddings exist. Page number 9.

**120.10.unions.** Empty set plus binary-union closure is equivalent to finite-union closure by induction on the number of summands (the zero-summand case is exactly ∅). For moderate spaces this transfers through a model chart.

**120.10.empty.** The empty model exists by M5; the unique function from it has empty graph and is moderate. Any two empty models have the unique bijection between them, moderate in both directions, giving the same transported empty structure.

**120.10.gluing.** For a finite cover X=∪X_i by moderate subsets, a function is moderate if and only if all restrictions are: restriction intersects its graph with X_i×Y, while conversely the graph is the finite union of the restriction graphs. Compatible maps on pieces glue uniquely as functions when they agree on pairwise intersections. Thus the asserted amalgamation property follows under M5.

The diagram has Z written over Y; the following sentence still says Y=∅, a clear unrevised old letter retained as written. The small category-family subscript at the end is a contracted star-like mark; interpreted consistently with M_* elsewhere after one crop, not silently treated as a new M1 category. The general pushout question is recorded as a question, without an existence claim.""",checks=[('120.10.unions','targeted proof check','Induction gives finite unions from empty and binary unions; the converse is immediate including the empty union.'),('120.10.empty','targeted proof check','Empty graphs are moderate by M5, so the empty model is initial and transported structure is unique.'),('120.10.gluing','targeted proof check','Restriction graphs are intersections; their finite union is the full graph. Compatibility on overlaps gives unique underlying glued map.')],habits=['Overwritten Z retains the upper fork of Y on scan 010. The later Y=∅ was not revised and stays Y; this is a revision mismatch, not a reason to normalize both names.'],notation=[('M5, later use','From scan 010 M5 denotes finite-union closure; the earlier scan 007 M5 meant R0≠∅. Both written labels are retained.')],abbreviations=[('esp. mod.','espace modéré'),('ssi','si et seulement si')],doubts=[('cancelled sign in axiom',r'\unsure{\delta}','looped cancelled sign','low')])
